{"skill_id":"first-order-sys","version":2,"questions":[{"id":"first-order-sys-r1-q2","version":1,"round":1,"type":"numeric","prompt":"The plant \\(6\\dot{y} + y = 2u\\) starts at rest. The input steps to 4 and stays there. The steady output is","answer":8.0,"unit":"1","tolerance":0.02,"explanation":"At steady state the derivative is zero, so \\(y = 2u = 2 \\times 4 = 8\\). The 6 never enters the steady value. Dividing the gain by 6 gives \\(4/3\\), and multiplying the input by 6 gives 24.","figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 340 176\" role=\"img\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\"><title>step of a first-order plant</title><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"318\" y2=\"146\"/><polygon points=\"318,146 311.6,148.7 311.6,143.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"46\" y2=\"24\"/><polygon points=\"46,24 48.7,30.4 43.3,30.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"318\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">t</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">y</text><polyline points=\"46,132.9 49,127.8 52,122.9 55.1,118.4 58.1,114 61.1,109.9 64.1,106.1 67.2,102.4 70.2,99 73.2,95.7 76.2,92.6 79.2,89.7 82.3,86.9 85.3,84.3 88.3,81.8 91.3,79.4 94.4,77.2 97.4,75.1 100.4,73.1 103.4,71.3 106.4,69.5 109.5,67.8 112.5,66.2 115.5,64.7 118.5,63.3 121.6,61.9 124.6,60.7 127.6,59.5 130.6,58.3 133.6,57.2 136.7,56.2 139.7,55.3 142.7,54.3 145.7,53.5 148.8,52.7 151.8,51.9 154.8,51.2 157.8,50.5 160.8,49.8 163.9,49.2 166.9,48.6 169.9,48.1 172.9,47.5 176,47 179,46.6 182,46.1 185,45.7 188,45.3 191.1,44.9 194.1,44.6 197.1,44.3 200.1,43.9 203.2,43.6 206.2,43.4 209.2,43.1 212.2,42.8 215.2,42.6 218.3,42.4 221.3,42.1 224.3,41.9 227.3,41.7 230.4,41.6 233.4,41.4 236.4,41.2 239.4,41.1 242.4,40.9 245.5,40.8 248.5,40.7 251.5,40.5 254.5,40.4 257.6,40.3 260.6,40.2 263.6,40.1 266.6,40 269.6,39.9 272.7,39.8 275.7,39.8 278.7,39.7 281.7,39.6 284.8,39.6 287.8,39.5 290.8,39.4 293.8,39.4 296.8,39.3 299.9,39.3 302.9,39.2 305.9,39.2 308.9,39.1 312,39.1 315,39.1 318,39\" stroke-width=\"2.2\"/></svg>","figure_alt":"A smooth curve that rises toward a horizontal line."},{"id":"first-order-sys-r1-q3","version":1,"round":1,"type":"numeric","prompt":"A first-order step response starts at rest. At \\(t\\) equal to one time constant, what fraction of the steady value has been reached?","answer":0.632121,"unit":"1","tolerance":0.02,"explanation":"From rest, \\(y(t) = y_\\infty(1 - e^{-t/\\tau})\\). At \\(t = \\tau\\) the exponent is \\(-1\\), so the fraction is \\(1 - e^{-1} = 0.632\\). Half would be a different definition. \\(e^{-1} = 0.368\\) is the fraction still missing, and \\(1 - e^{-2}\\) is two time constants.","figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 340 176\" role=\"img\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\"><title>one time constant of rise</title><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"318\" y2=\"146\"/><polygon points=\"318,146 311.6,148.7 311.6,143.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"46\" y2=\"24\"/><polygon points=\"46,24 48.7,30.4 43.3,30.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"318\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">t</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">y</text><polyline points=\"46,132.9 49,127.8 52,122.9 55.1,118.4 58.1,114 61.1,109.9 64.1,106.1 67.2,102.4 70.2,99 73.2,95.7 76.2,92.6 79.2,89.7 82.3,86.9 85.3,84.3 88.3,81.8 91.3,79.4 94.4,77.2 97.4,75.1 100.4,73.1 103.4,71.3 106.4,69.5 109.5,67.8 112.5,66.2 115.5,64.7 118.5,63.3 121.6,61.9 124.6,60.7 127.6,59.5 130.6,58.3 133.6,57.2 136.7,56.2 139.7,55.3 142.7,54.3 145.7,53.5 148.8,52.7 151.8,51.9 154.8,51.2 157.8,50.5 160.8,49.8 163.9,49.2 166.9,48.6 169.9,48.1 172.9,47.5 176,47 179,46.6 182,46.1 185,45.7 188,45.3 191.1,44.9 194.1,44.6 197.1,44.3 200.1,43.9 203.2,43.6 206.2,43.4 209.2,43.1 212.2,42.8 215.2,42.6 218.3,42.4 221.3,42.1 224.3,41.9 227.3,41.7 230.4,41.6 233.4,41.4 236.4,41.2 239.4,41.1 242.4,40.9 245.5,40.8 248.5,40.7 251.5,40.5 254.5,40.4 257.6,40.3 260.6,40.2 263.6,40.1 266.6,40 269.6,39.9 272.7,39.8 275.7,39.8 278.7,39.7 281.7,39.6 284.8,39.6 287.8,39.5 290.8,39.4 293.8,39.4 296.8,39.3 299.9,39.3 302.9,39.2 305.9,39.2 308.9,39.1 312,39.1 315,39.1 318,39\" stroke-width=\"2.2\"/></svg>","figure_alt":"A smooth curve that rises toward a horizontal line."},{"id":"first-order-sys-r2-q1","version":1,"round":2,"type":"numeric","prompt":"A free response (input held at 0) starts at \\(y(0) = 6\\). The time constant is 2 s. The value at \\(t = 2\\) s is","answer":2.20728,"unit":"1","tolerance":0.02,"explanation":"Free motion is \\(y(t) = 6 e^{-t/2}\\). At \\(t = 2\\) the exponent is \\(-1\\), so \\(y = 6/e = 2.207\\). Using \\(t\\) itself as the exponent gives \\(6e^{-2}\\). Halving because one time constant passed gives 3, and that is a straight line, not an exponential.","figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 340 176\" role=\"img\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\"><title>free decay</title><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"318\" y2=\"146\"/><polygon points=\"318,146 311.6,148.7 311.6,143.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"46\" y2=\"24\"/><polygon points=\"46,24 48.7,30.4 43.3,30.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"318\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">t</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">y</text><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"134.6\" x2=\"318\" y2=\"134.6\" stroke-dash