\"114\" y2=\"90\"/><line x1=\"142\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"280\" y2=\"90\"/><polygon points=\"280,90 273.6,92.7 273.6,87.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"150\" y1=\"160\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"16\"/><polygon points=\"150,16 152.7,22.4 147.3,22.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"274\" y=\"106\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Re</text><text x=\"158\" y=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Im</text><line x1=\"123\" y1=\"85\" x2=\"133\" y2=\"95\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"/><line x1=\"123\" y1=\"95\" x2=\"133\" y2=\"85\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"/></svg>","figure_alt":"One pole mark on the real axis, left of the origin."},{"id":"first-order-sys-r3-q3","version":1,"round":3,"type":"numeric","prompt":"From rest, \\(y(t) = 9(1 - e^{-t/3})\\). The slope \\(\\dot{y}\\) at \\(t = 0\\) is","answer":3.0,"unit":"1/s","tolerance":0.02,"explanation":"Differentiate: \\(\\dot{y} = 9 \\cdot (1/3) e^{-t/3}\\). At \\(t = 0\\) the exponential is 1, so the slope is \\(9/3 = 3\\). The 9 is the steady value, not the slope. \\(9 \\times 3 = 27\\) multiplies by the time constant instead of dividing. \\(1/3\\) is the decay rate of the missing piece, not the initial slope of this particular step.","figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 340 176\" role=\"img\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\"><title>initial slope of a rise</title><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"318\" y2=\"146\"/><polygon points=\"318,146 311.6,148.7 311.6,143.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"46\" y2=\"24\"/><polygon points=\"46,24 48.7,30.4 43.3,30.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"318\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">t</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"cur