with a leading coefficient. The pole is \\(-1/\\tau\\) only after \\(\\tau\\) is that coefficient. The step formula uses both numbers, so it is last. Reading the pole from \\(K\\) swaps the speed with the resting level.","figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 340 176\" role=\"img\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\"><title>first-order rise</title><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"318\" y2=\"146\"/><polygon points=\"318,146 311.6,148.7 311.6,143.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"46\" y2=\"24\"/><polygon points=\"46,24 48.7,30.4 43.3,30.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"318\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">t</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">y</text><polyline points=\"46,132.9 49,127.8 52,122.9 55.1,118.4 58.1,114 61.1,109.9 64.1,106.1 67.2,102.4 70.2,99 73.2,95.7 76.2,92.6 79.2,89.7 82.3,86.9 85.3,84.3 88.3,81.8 91.3,79.4 94.4,77.2 97.4,75.1 100.4,73.1 103.4,71.3 106.4,69.5 109.5,67.8 112.5,66.2 115.5,64.7 118.5,63.3 121.6,61.9 124.6,60.7 127.6,59.5 130.6,58.3 133.6,57.2 136.7,56.2 139.7,55.3 142.7,54.3 145.7,53.5 148.8,52.7 151.8,51.9 154.8,51.2 157.8,50.5 160.8,49.8 163.9,49.2 166.9,48.6 169.9,48.1 172.9,47.5 176,47 179,46.6 182,46.1 185,45.7 188,45.3 191.1,44.9 194.1,44.6 197.1,44.3 200.1,43.9 203.2,43.6 206.2,43.4 209.2,43.1 212.2,42.8 215.2,42.6 218.3,42.4 221.3,42.1 224.3,41.9 227.3,41.7 230.4,41.6 233.4,41.4 236.4,41.2 239.4,41.1 242.4,40.9 245.5,40.8 248.5,40.7 251.5,40.5 254.5,40.4 257.6,40.3 260.6,40.2 263.6,40.1 266.6,40 269.6,39.9 272.7,39.8 275.7,39.8 278.7,39.7 281.7,39.6 284.8,39.6 287.8,39.5 290.8,39.4 293.8,39.4 296.8,39.3 299.9,39.3 302.9,39.2 305.9,39.2 308.9,39.1 312,39.1 315,39.1 318,39\" stroke-width=\"2.2\"/></svg>","figure_alt":"A smooth curve that rises toward a horizontal line and does not overshoot.","steps":["Scale the equation so the coefficient of \\(y\\) is 1.","Read \\(\\tau\\) as the coefficient of \\(\\dot y\\), and \\(K\\) as the coefficient of \\(u\\).","Place the single pole at \\(-1/\\tau\\).","From rest, a constant input \\(u\\) settles at \\(Ku\\) along \\(Ku(1-e^{-t/\\tau})\\)."]},{"id":"first-order-sys-r2-q4","version":1,"round":2,"type":"symbolic","prompt":"A first-order output starts at \\(y_i\\) and a constant input would settle it at \\(y_f\\). The time constant is \\(\\tau\\). For \\(t>0\\), write \\(y(t)\\) using the names \\(yi\\), \\(yf\\), \\(tau\\), and \\(t\\).","answer":"yf+(yi-yf)*exp(-t/tau)","tolerance":0.001,"explanation":"The gap \\(yi-yf\\) shrinks by \\(e^{-t/\\tau}\\). Adding that shrinking gap to the final value starts at \\(yi\\) and ends at \\(yf\\). Using \\(yi\\,e^{-t/\\tau}\\) alone is the free response, which heads to 0. Swapping \\(yi\\) and \\(yf\\) starts at the wrong end.","figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 340 176\" role=\"img\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\"><title>free response</title><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"318\" y2=\"146\"/><polygon points=\"318,146 311.6,148.7 311.6,143.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"46\" y2=\"24\"/><polygon points=\"46,24 48.7,30.4 43.3,30.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"318\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">t</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">y</text><polyline points=\"46,39 49,42.8 52,46.5 55.1,50 58.1,53.4 61.1,56.6 64.1,59.8 67.2,62.8 70.2,65.6 73.2,68.4 76.2,71.1 79.2,73.6 82.3,76 85.3,78.4 88.3,80.7 91.3,82.8 94.4,84.9 97.4,86.9 100.4,88.8 103.4,90.7 106.4,92.4 109.5,94.1 112.5,95.8 115.5,97.3 118.5,98.9 121.6,100.3 124.6,