is \\(-\\tau\\), not \\(-1\\).","The output is already at the final value when \\(t=\\tau\\)."],"correct_reason":0},{"id":"first-order-sys-r4-q4","version":1,"round":4,"type":"numeric","prompt":"Two first-order systems have the same DC gain. Their time constants are \\(\\tau_1=1\\ \\mathrm{s}\\) and \\(\\tau_2=4\\ \\mathrm{s}\\). How long does the slower one take to reach 95% of its final value after a step from rest?","answer":11.9829,"unit":"s","tolerance":0.02,"explanation":"The slower time constant is 4 s. Ninety-five percent means \\(e^{-t/\\tau}=0.05\\), so \\(t=\\tau\\ln 20\\). That is \\(4\\ln 20\\) seconds. Using \\(\\tau=1\\) answers the faster system. One time constant is the 63% point.","preview":["lti-circuits"],"figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 340 176\" role=\"img\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\"><title>first-order rise</title><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"318\" y2=\"146\"/><polygon points=\"318,146 311.6,148.7 311.6,143.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"46\" y2=\"24\"/><polygon points=\"46,24 48.7,30.4 43.3,30.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"318\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">t</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">y</text><polyline points=\"46,132.9 49,127.8 52,122.9 55.1,118.4 58.1,114 61.1,109.9 64.1,106.1 67.2,102.4 70.2,99 73.2,95.7 76.2,92.6 79.2,89.7 82.3,86.9 85.3,84.3 88.3,81.8 91.3,79.4 94.4,77.2 97.4,75.1 100.4,73.1 103.4,71.3 106.4,69.5 109.5,67.8 112.5,66.2 115.5,64.7 118.5,63.3 121.6,61.9 124.6,60.7 127.6,59.5 130.6,58.3 133.6,57.2 136.7,56.2 139.7,55.3 142.7,54.3 145.7,53.5 148.8,52.7 151.8,51.9 154.8,51.2 157.8,50.5 160.8,49.8 163.9,49.2 166.9,48.6 169.9,48.1 172.9,47.5 176,47 179,46.6 182,46.1 185,45.7 188,45.3 191.1,44.9 194.1,4